   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Working life, from contract to deadline",
     "texto": [
      "**Two ways of working.** **Por cuenta ajena**: you are an employee. **Por cuenta propia**: you are self-employed.\n\n**In the office.** **El equipo**, **la jefa**, **el cliente**. **La reunión**, **el informe**, **el plazo**, **la entrega**.\n\n**Contract and hours.** A **contrato indefinido** has no end date. The **jornada** can be continuous or split. Many companies offer **horario flexible** and **teletrabajo**.\n\n**Pay.** The **nómina** shows what you earn each month. In Spain two **pagas extra** are paid a year.\n\n**Moving up.** **Ascender** and **el ascenso**.\n\n**Deadlines.** **Cumplir con** the deadline, **entregar** the report on time, **retrasarse**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Llevar + time, desde hace and mientras",
     "texto": [
      "**Llevar + time + gerund** tells how long something that continues has lasted: **llevamos dos semanas trabajando**, **lleva un año viviendo aquí**.\n\n**Desde hace + time** says how long something has been going on: **trabajo aquí desde hace tres años**. With a date, **desde** is used: **desde el lunes**.\n\n**Mientras + subjunctive** means «for as long as» and talks about the future: **mientras no haya un plan, seguirá el retraso**. When it talks about the present, the indicative is used: **mientras trabajo, escucho música**."
     ],
